<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sonny Liston returns four weeks after starting amlodipine 5 mg and valsartan 160 mg. He has taken it every morning and can say what it is for and when to take it. He did not send home readings for the first two weeks: the clinic had asked him to photograph the monitor and send the picture, and the steps on the phone were confusing. After a nurse called him in the third week he began reading the numbers out on the clinic voice line; the last seven mornings average 134/84 mmHg. No dizziness or ankle swelling. Drinking is down to about 15 drinks a week, but he still has five or six on Saturday nights and finds he cannot stop once he starts; he asks for the medicine he was told about. No thoughts of suicide. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home readings</td><td>Average 134/84 mmHg over the last seven mornings</td></tr><tr><td>Potassium and creatinine</td><td>4.4 mmol/L and 1.1 mg/dL</td></tr><tr><td>AUDIT-C</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Teach-back</td><td>Correct with the picture card</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

