    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension, stage 2 (I10)</content>. Better but above the goal of under 130/80 mmHg in the clinic and at home; potassium and creatinine unchanged on valsartan. [S]<list><item>Raise to amlodipine 10 mg and valsartan 160 mg in one tablet each morning; new picture card.</item><item>Home readings each morning by voice message.</item><item>Still no bouts until controlled.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, moderate (F10.20)</content>. Progress, with loss of control on weekend nights; he chose naltrexone after the options were explained again. Liver tests at intake were well below the level that would rule it out, and he takes no opioids. [S]<list><item>Naltrexone 50 mg each morning.</item><item>A wallet card saying he takes naltrexone, which blocks opioid pain medicines, for any emergency.</item><item>Liver tests in about two months.</item><item>Keep the tally card and his drinking goal.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure (seated, large cuff, average of two readings), weight and BMI, heart sounds</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136/86 mmHg; weight 98.0 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Out-of-office blood pressure (ambulatory or home monitoring)</td><td>At diagnosis and after each treatment change</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Deviation: home readings were asked for each morning from the start of treatment but none arrived for two weeks, because the photo-upload steps were not usable for him and teach-back had not covered them. Office and later home readings agree, so no harm is known. Corrective action: readings by voice message, shown with teach-back by the nurse; seven readings in the last week averaged 134/84 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Potassium, creatinine and eGFR</td><td>Baseline; two to four weeks after starting an ARB; then every six months on an ARB</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Potassium 4.4 mmol/L, creatinine 1.1 mg/dL, eGFR 89, four weeks after starting valsartan; next in about six months</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipids, glucose or A1c, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, TSH</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly (TSH at diagnosis)</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done at intake; next yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>At diagnosis for stage 2 hypertension or suspected LVH; repeat as indicated</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Mild LVH at two weeks; repeat in about a year to look for regression with control</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antihypertensive tolerance (ankle edema, dizziness) and adherence by teach-back</td><td>Each follow-up and each dose change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No dizziness or edema on 5/160 mg; teach-back correct; dose raised today with a new picture card</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Fitness to compete (AHA/ACC athlete statement)</td><td>At diagnosis and before returning to competition</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Not yet controlled; no bouts</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Drinking (AUDIT-C, drinks per week, drinking days)</td><td>Every follow-up during treatment; full AUDIT at about four months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 7; about 15 drinks a week, with heavy Saturday nights</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Liver tests (AST, ALT, GGT)</td><td>Baseline; about two months after starting naltrexone or cutting down; then as indicated</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Intake AST 46, ALT 38, GGT 88 U/L; recheck in about two months on naltrexone</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Naltrexone: nausea, liver tests, and opioid-blockade wallet card</td><td>Each follow-up after starting</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Started today; no opioid use; wallet 